- [900](../issues/900-neural-representation-lab.md), T10; [T07](../issues-done/900-NRL-0013-calibration-and-resumable-local-training.done), [T08](../issues-done/900-NRL-0014-evaluate-benchmark-and-compare.done), [T09](../issues-done/900-NRL-0015-mixed-plans-and-bounded-search.done).

## Resolution

Implemented `research/recovery.rs`, actual train-only student trajectories, original teacher FFNs on the same inputs, simultaneous local SGD, matched original-input control and earliest full-model validation selection. Pair/run hashes, every round, whole-logit error, standalone models, compatible benchmarks and separate held-out metrics are saved and recomputed by independent recovery/check/replay tools. All **70 host tests**, both portable rlibs and complete CLI cycles passed on `5edd9bc6`. [Evidence](../nrl/reports/recovery-2026-10-26.json), [complete saved run](../nrl/reports/recovery-example-2026-10-26/complete.json), [contract](../nrl/specs/student-recovery-v0.md).

Both arms select round 3. Student-input recovery improves validation NLL from 4.010611310636807 to 4.010565653753475 (original-input control: 4.010594939048665). It still exceeds the dense baseline 2.792273884144422 and the pre-frozen quality budget. Held-out perplexity is 105.0541886201988 versus dense 9.35922873023494. The deployment recommendation remains **dense** despite lower observed forward time. This is a valid negative compression result on the miniature corpus, not end-to-end decoder backpropagation, representative language quality or native performance evidence. T06–T10 are complete for the declared bounded host profiles; native integration and broader optimization/families remain T11–T13. Full landing gate is pending.
